00:53:55.320 --> 00:54:01.400
So, we like symmetry and beauty.

00:54:01.400 --> 00:54:02.400
And that's fine.

00:54:02.400 --> 00:54:03.720
That’s all the way across the animal kingdom.

00:54:03.720 --> 00:54:04.720
So butterflies.

00:54:04.720 --> 00:54:08.580
There are butterflies that wont mate with
another butterfly if it deviates from symmetry

00:54:08.580 --> 00:54:10.680
some absurdly tiny amount.

00:54:10.680 --> 00:54:14.980
Like really, it’s micro measurement deviation.

00:54:14.980 --> 00:54:20.990
I gues they have a butterfly template and
if you know, the potential mating butterfly

00:54:20.990 --> 00:54:23.560
doesn't match, it’s like flitter off.

00:54:23.560 --> 00:54:26.160
You’re not getting anywhere.

00:54:26.160 --> 00:54:28.320
So, that's fine.

00:54:28.320 --> 00:54:29.320
So symmetry.

00:54:29.320 --> 00:54:33.990
This researcher, god only knows what possessed
him, took a bunch of men, ranging from symmetrical

00:54:33.990 --> 00:54:38.609
to asymmetrical - judged by a panel - and
