00:57:50.230 --> 00:57:51.440
Something like that.

00:57:51.440 --> 00:57:55.480
So anyways, that’s quite remarkable.

00:57:55.480 --> 00:58:00.320
Now back to the rats and the expectancy model.

00:58:00.320 --> 00:58:06.349
We already know that you can get an orienting
response out of a human being if something

00:58:06.349 --> 00:58:07.470
deviates from expectancy.

00:58:07.470 --> 00:58:13.520
Now people started studying this in rats,
and the original conceptualization was expectation.

00:58:13.520 --> 00:58:17.490
So you have an expectation about how the world
is gonna lay itself out.

00:58:17.490 --> 00:58:22.510
That’s your model, and then if the world
deviates from that, you have an orienting

00:58:22.510 --> 00:58:27.070
reflex and what that does is protect you from
predation.

00:58:27.070 --> 00:58:30.190
That’s the first level of the orienting
response.

00:58:30.190 --> 00:58:31.829
It’s really, really primitive.

00:58:31.829 --> 00:58:36.000
It’s mediated only by a few neuronal connections
so it’s unbelievably rapid.

00:58:36.000 --> 00:58:41.820
Then after that, there’s anxiety and the
proclivity to explore.

00:58:41.820 --> 00:58:42.960
That both gets activated.

00:58:42.960 --> 00:58:50.579
So it’s first protective, then you orient
towards the - imagine you're walking down

00:58:50.579 --> 00:58:52.579
the street and hear a really loud noise behind
you.

00:58:52.579 --> 00:58:54.990
It’s like really loud, so it startles you.

00:58:54.990 --> 00:58:59.300
Well you go into a crouch so that if a tiger
had jumped on your back, it would be hard

00:58:59.300 --> 00:59:06.250
for it to get your neck, and then tenths of
a second later, you'll turn assuming you don't

00:59:06.250 --> 00:59:11.700
get attacked by a tiger, you’ll swivel and
turn and orient all your senses towards the

00:59:11.700 --> 00:59:18.010
locale that was specified by the sound because
you have a stereo auditory system and you

00:59:18.010 --> 00:59:21.640
can localize events in space using that.

00:59:21.640 --> 00:59:23.920
So you orient towards it - that’s part of
the orienting reflex.

00:59:23.920 --> 00:59:25.230
It’s a reflex.

00:59:25.230 --> 00:59:26.460
It’s not voluntary.

00:59:26.460 --> 00:59:32.170
So, and then once you've got your eyes trained
on it, and your ears, then you start to explore

00:59:32.170 --> 00:59:36.230
it and then you might freeze.

00:59:36.230 --> 00:59:39.590
You might get out of there which is a panic
response.

00:59:39.590 --> 00:59:42.440
That’s another thing that could be triggered
by the orienting reflex.

00:59:42.440 --> 00:59:43.440
Different circuit.

00:59:43.440 --> 00:59:45.340
Or you might think, “Wow, what’s going
on over there?

00:59:45.340 --> 00:59:46.790
It looks interesting.”

00:59:46.790 --> 00:59:48.470
And then you go approach it.

00:59:48.470 --> 00:59:55.710
Now, those two - the exploratory part is mediated
in part by the hypothalamus which is a very

00:59:55.710 --> 01:00:01.510
very old system, and it has a whole section,
about half of it is devoted to the circuitry

01:00:01.510 --> 01:00:05.320
that you would use to figure out what was
going on if something that you didn't understood

01:00:05.320 --> 01:00:06.320
happened.

01:00:06.320 --> 01:00:10.660
And then you have a whole other circuit that’s
hippocampal and amygdalic that regulates the

01:00:10.660 --> 01:00:14.960
exploratory circuit and says be careful because
while you're gathering information, you might

01:00:14.960 --> 01:00:21.750
get killed and the anxiety circuit takes primacy,
generally speaking, over the exploratory circuit.

01:00:21.750 --> 01:00:26.920
And the reason for that is you don't want
to get information and be dead so caution

01:00:26.920 --> 01:00:28.090
is the watchword.

01:00:28.090 --> 01:00:32.839
Now, the other thing you might think about
which is an extremely useful thing to think

01:00:32.839 --> 01:00:33.950
about.

01:00:33.950 --> 01:00:36.820
Okay let’s go back to that diagram I showed
you with the hierarchy.

01:00:36.820 --> 01:00:41.360
Right, so you’ve got the motor actions at
the bottom, and you've got the high level

01:00:41.360 --> 01:00:43.100
abstractions at the top.

